   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Greeting people",
     "texto": [
      "**Ciao** is informal and works both for saying hello and for saying goodbye.",
      "More formal: **buongiorno** is used during the day, and **buonasera** from the afternoon or at dusk; when the change happens varies by place and situation.",
      "To say goodbye: **arrivederci**. Before going to sleep: **buonanotte**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Informal and formal «you»",
     "texto": [
      "**Tu** means «you» (informal). To address someone formally you use **Lei**, which takes the same verb form as «she»: **Lei si chiama**. Writing **Lei** with a capital letter is an optional politeness convention; you will also see **lei**.",
      "To say your name: **Mi chiamo Anna** (my name is Anna) or **Sono Anna** (I am Anna).",
      "To ask it: **Come ti chiami?** (informal) or **Come si chiama?** (formal).",
      "When you meet someone: **Piacere** (nice to meet you)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
